mode: "100644"
text: "# Stories 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (Instagram/Facebook ship Stories changes often).*\n\n## The point: relationship engine, not reach\nInstagram's own leadership (Mosseri) is explicit: **Stories are not your best tool for reaching new\npeople** — they're the **relationship-deepening engine** for *existing* followers. Sticker taps,\nreplies, and viewing history feed a **relationship signal** that bumps you to the front of someone's\ntray *and* lifts your Feed/Reels ranking for them. So optimise for **intimacy + interaction**, not reach.\n\n## Metrics that matter\n**Completion rate, exits, replies, sticker taps, link taps, profile visits** — not impressions alone.\n(Instagram unified surface counts under \"Views\" in 2026, but exits/taps remain the diagnostic.) Pair\nwith business outcomes (DMs, sign-ups, sales) for ROI.\n\n## Interactive stickers — the single most effective tool\nThey turn passive viewers into **tappers** (a strong relationship signal) and double as audience research:\n- **Poll / slider** — quick feedback, low-friction votes.\n- **Quiz** (one correct answer) — educate, segment beginners vs advanced, product fit.\n- **Question box** — invites replies; spin answers into an AMA follow-up sequence (lands in DMs).\n- **Countdown** — a *real* deadline; tap-to-subscribe builds a warm retarget list.\n- **Link sticker** (all accounts) — pair with an explicit **\"Tap here\"** overlay; **\"add yours\"** /\n  **cutout** for participation. Reshare UGC tags as social proof.\n\n## Structure + sequence\nPer sequence: **hook (problem/outcome) → one proof point/step → an interactive sticker → one clear\nnext step.** **One goal per sequence** — don't ask three things. Build **3–5 frame arcs** / multi-day\nmini-series; **one beat per frame**, each a distinct takeaway. Reply to Story replies **via DM** — the\nreal relationship (and the strongest distribution signal overall).\n\n## Specs + cadence\n**9:16, 1080×1920**; keep key content in the **safe zone (1080×1420)**, clear of UI; video segments run\nup to **60s each** (longer uploads auto-split; photos display ~5s) — keep one beat ~15s; images <4MB,\nvideo <30MB (scheduler limits); **text sparingly**; **sound-off legible**, strong first frame.\n**Daily** posting, ~**3–7 frames/day** (consistency > volume). Content mix ~**70% value / 20%\nbehind-the-scenes / 10% promo.**\n\n## Close Friends — the intimacy lever\nThe **Close Friends** list (green ring) is a top-practitioner move, not just a personal feature: share\n**insider/VIP content** — early access, soft launches, raw BTS, exclusive offers — to a hand-built list of\nwarmest followers/customers. The green ring itself earns the tap (scarcity + belonging), and it's the\nclosest thing Stories has to a free \"inner circle\" tier. Invite people in via a public Story (\"want in?\nreply and I'll add you\") to build the list with consent.\n\n## Highlights + cross-format\n**Highlights** make proven sequences **evergreen** (add context) — the one durable lever on an\notherwise 24-hour surface. Stories are **spokes** off Reels/carousel hubs (repurpose a carousel slide\ninto a Story with a sticker the next day) — ties to `content-recycling` / `cross-platform-repurposing`.\n\n## Facebook Stories\nSame mechanics (stickers, polls, links, 24h). WoopSocial supports IG + FB; IG is the primary surface.\n"
